 ## Deletion
 
-Deleting a member's account removes the member, and keeps each of their pantry orders with its member set to none.
-The food bank's grant requires seven years of order counts per pantry; in 2024 a deletion that removed a member's
-orders left a gap in the counts, and the grant's auditors flagged it. An order without a member holds an id and an
-amount, and identifies no one.
+[`delete_member`](../../larder/members.py) removes the member's account and all pantry orders linked to their member
+id. Other members and their pantry orders, and orders already without a member, remain.
+
+Orders were previously retained without a member for the food bank's grant audits. Deletion now removes the linked
+orders too, so those orders no longer contribute to the retained order counts.
